{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.twist_gram_selfAdjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.twist_gram_selfAdjoint","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**The twist knot operator is Gram-self-adjoint.** `G · σ²` is symmetric — its two\noff-diagonal entries agree, `(G·σ²)₀₁ = (G·σ²)₁₀` — so `σ²` is self-adjoint in the Markov\ninner product. This is the fact that makes the recurrence diagonalise: `G⁻¹` builds the\ndual / Jones–Wenzl projector basis on which `σ²` is diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.gram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.gram","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The Markov-pairing **Gram matrix** on `{1, e}`: `G = !![δ, 1; 1, δ]`\n(`⟨1,1⟩ = tr_M 1 = δ`, `⟨1,e⟩ = tr_M e = 1`, `⟨e,e⟩ = tr_M(δe) = δ`). Symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.twist","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L86-L88","doc":"The **twist operator** `σ²` — one full clasp twist, the knot operator of the twist-knot\nfamily. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.braid","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The Kauffman braiding `σ = A·1 + u·e` (here the inverse strand weight is the ring\nelement `u`, so the statement stays over a generic commutative ring rather than a field). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.eGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.eGen","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L79-L80","doc":"The Temperley–Lieb cup-cap generator `e` on `{1, e}` (left multiplication), `e² = δe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.trace_two_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.trace_two_step","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L65-L73","doc":"**Closure / Markov-trace recurrence.** Applying the (linear) trace — the closure of the\ntangle, i.e. the knot invariant — to `pow_two_step` gives the invariant's two-term\nrecurrence: `tr(Mⁿ⁺²) = t·tr(Mⁿ⁺¹) − d·tr(Mⁿ)`. This is the twist-knot Jones-polynomial\nrecurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.pow_two_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.pow_two_step","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**Power recurrence.** If a knot operator `M` satisfies the quadratic relation\n`M·M = t·M − d·1` (its `2×2` Cayley–Hamilton), then its powers obey the two-term linear\nrecurrence `Mⁿ⁺² = t·Mⁿ⁺¹ − d·Mⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.charpoly_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotOperatorRecurrence.charpoly_two","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotOperatorRecurrence.lean#L45-L53","doc":"**2×2 Cayley–Hamilton.** Every `2×2` matrix satisfies its characteristic polynomial:\n`M·M = (M₀₀+M₁₁)·M − (M₀₀M₁₁ − M₀₁M₁₀)·1` — trace and determinant as the recurrence\ncoefficients. ","signatureChunk":0}]}